msgid "Testing virtual thread applications"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As mentioned above, virtual threads have a few limitations that can "
"drastically affect your application performance and memory usage.\n"
"The _junit-virtual-threads_ extension provides a way to detect pinned "
"carrier threads while running your tests.\n"
"Thus, you can eliminate one of the most prominent limitations or be aware of "
"the problem."
msgstr ""

msgid "To enable this detection:"
msgstr ""

msgid "1) Add the `junit-virtual-threads` dependency to your project:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"2) In your test case, add the `io.quarkus.test.junit.virtual."
"VirtualThreadUnit`  and `io.quarkus.test.junit.virtual.ShouldNotPin` "
"annotations:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you run your test (remember to use Java 21+), Quarkus detects pinned "
"carrier threads.\n"
"When it happens, the test fails."
msgstr ""

msgid "The `@ShouldNotPin` can also be used on methods directly."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The _junit-virtual-threads_ also provides a `@ShouldPin` annotation for "
"cases where pinning is unavoidable.\n"
"The following snippet demonstrates the `@ShouldPin` annotation usage."
msgstr ""

